# Step 2, GET /ask?sku=abc: ask the model, offering the tools. The answer
# lands under `_turn`: `text`, `finish`, `tool_calls` (each with its
# arguments and the offered tool's binding) and `message` (the assistant
# turn, ready to append to the next request).
#
# The scope's mock-response.json is the model's first answer when the
# request asks for mocks (X-Txco-Mocks: front/200/*): one call to
# stock_check. Without the header the same rule asks OpenAI (OPENAI_KEY).
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path == "/ask" && ._tools.count == 2
  WITH system   = "You answer questions about a small shop. Use the tools for facts; never guess stock.",
       prompt   = "Is SKU {{@web.req.url.query.sku.0}} in stock?",
       tools    = ._tools.tools,
       provider = "openai",
       into     = "_turn"
  EXEC "ai://chat"
